# Cloudflare Pages security headers for GlassBox
#
# Deliberately minimal. GlassBox's whole job is to measure which browser
# features/APIs are exposed, so a restrictive Permissions-Policy would corrupt
# its own readings (features it probes would report as unavailable). And because
# the app is one self-contained file with inline <script> and <style>, a strict
# CSP would need 'unsafe-inline' to work at all, which defeats the point — so CSP
# is omitted rather than added for show. These four are safe and don't break any
# probe (cross-origin images, STUN, and the geo fetches all still work).

/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: no-referrer
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
